course: dictionary
lesson: 14984
title: Replenishment: filling up again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some long words are built from parts you already know. Replenish means to fill something up again. The ending -ment often turns a verb into a noun, a word for an action or a thing. So replenishment is the act of filling something up again, and it can also mean the new supply that does the filling.
explain: «After the dry summer, the rain brought replenishment to the lake.» The dry weather had left the lake low, and the rain filled it back up. Try your meaning in the sentence: "the rain brought filling up again to the lake" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: «The shop's replenishment of stocks happens every morning.» Here the clue is shop, and shelves that run low. Replenishment is about putting new goods out so the shelves are full again. Words like this are often used for things that run out, such as water, food, or pencils.
fact: Replenish means to fill something up again after it has been used or emptied.
fact: The ending -ment often turns a verb into a noun, so replenishment is the action of replenishing.
fact: Replenishment can also mean the new supply that fills something up.
fact: «Water replenishment» means water refilling a lake or an underground store, often after rain.
fact: Replenishment is mostly uncountable, so we say «some replenishment», not «a replenishment».
exercise: «The lake was low, so the rain brought water replenishment.» What does replenishment mean here? | Emptying it out | * Filling it up again | Making it colder | Drying the ground
exercise: «Every morning the shopkeeper does the replenishment of the shelves.» What is the shopkeeper doing? | Counting the money only | Painting the shop | * Putting out new stock to fill the shelves again | Taking all the stock away
exercise: Which everyday job is an example of replenishment? | Reading a book about pencils | Losing your pencil case | * Filling your pencil case with new pencils | Breaking a pencil in half
test: «After the long hot day, the body needs replenishment of water.» What does this mean? | * The body gets new water to replace what it lost | The body is painted blue | The body loses all its water | The body stops needing water
test: Which word is the root that replenishment comes from? | * replenish | enjoy | shelf | ruin
exam: Which sentence uses replenishment correctly? | The replenishment is a loud, bright song | * The rain brought replenishment to the dry lake | The replenishment ran very fast up the hill | Replenishment is the colour of the sky
